        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Express <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\log_3(2)+\\log_3(5)]</span> as a single logarithm.  </p>",
            "readable_text": "Express [MATH: \\log_3(2)+\\log_3(5)] as a single logarithm.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, let&#x27;s recall the product rule for logarithms:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\log_n a + \\log_n b = \\log_n(ab)]</span></p><p>Using the product rule for logarithms, the given expression can be rewritten as</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\log_{3} 2 + \\log_{3} 5|= \\log_{3} (2 \u22c5 5); = \\log_{3} 10.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n[MATH: \\log_n a + \\log_n b = \\log_n(ab)]\n\nUsing the product rule for logarithms, the given expression can be rewritten as\n\n[MATH: \\log_{3} 2 + \\log_{3} 5|= \\log_{3} (2 \u22c5 5); = \\log_{3} 10.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nExpress [MATH: \\log_3(2)+\\log_3(5)] as a single logarithm.\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n[MATH: \\log_n a + \\log_n b = \\log_n(ab)]\n\nUsing the product rule for logarithms, the given expression can be rewritten as\n\n[MATH: \\log_{3} 2 + \\log_{3} 5|= \\log_{3} (2 \u22c5 5); = \\log_{3} 10.]"
      },
